Package: orchrd
Title: PowerShell-Inspired Workflow Orchestration for R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Lawrence", "Garba",
           email = "yayoli@infosights.ng",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = ""))
Description: Makes R pipelines production-grade. Run things (run_cmd,
    run_script, run_bg, await), chain them (pipe_exec, with_rollback),
    retry them (retry, retry_labeled), log them (log_step, with_log,
    log_config, get_log), and guard against failure before it happens
    (need, secret, health_check, notify). Includes reactive filesystem
    watchers and time-based schedule triggers backed by a compiled C++
    layer (inotify on Linux, ReadDirectoryChangesW on Windows, kqueue on
    macOS) via Rcpp, with composable guards (disk, memory, network) and
    throttling, plus tools for inspecting, configuring, debugging, and
    optimizing Docker infrastructure for R projects. Designed as workflow
    infrastructure for the openafrR African data ecosystem but general
    enough for any R developer orchestrating scripts, APIs, and deployments.
